<title>UK: IEA supply/demand highlights - end-Sept report.</title>
<headline>IEA supply/demand highlights - end-Sept report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table highlights the oil supply-demand and stock estimates included in the International Energy Agency's latest Monthly Oil Market Report. Figures in million barrels per day.</p>
<p>		  1994 1Q95 2Q95 3Q95 4Q95 1995 1Q96 2Q96 3Q96 4Q96 1996 1Q97 1997</p>
<p>DEMAND</p>
<p> OECD	   40.0 41.0 39.2 39.7 41.3 40.3 42.1 39.6 40.7 41.9 41.1 42.5 41.7</p>
<p> NON-OECD     28.9 30.2 29.1 29.0 30.6 29.8 30.8 30.0 30.0 31.8 30.7 32.2 32.0</p>
<p> TOTAL	  68.9 71.3 68.3 68.8 72.0 70.1 72.9 69.7 70.6 73.7 71.8 74.7 73.6</p>
<p>SUPPLY</p>
<p> NON-OPEC     41.6 42.4 42.0 42.4 42.7 42.4 43.2 43.2 43.5 45.0 43.7 45.3 45.5</p>
<p> OPEC CRUDE   27.0 27.2 27.3 27.6 27.8 27.6 28.2 28.2 28.6</p>
<p> OPEC NGLS     2.4  2.4  2.4  2.4  2.5  2.4  2.5  2.6  2.7  2.8  2.6  2.7  2.8</p>
<p> TOTAL OPEC   27.0 27.2 27.3 27.6 27.8 27.5 28.2 28.2</p>
<p>TOTAL SUPPLY 68.6 69.6 69.3 70.1 70.6 69.9 71.4 71.4 72.1</p>
<p> OPEC CALL*   24.9 26.5 23.9 23.9 26.7 25.3 27.2 23.9 24.5 25.9 25.4 26.7 25.3</p>
<p> IND STOCKS    +0.1 -1.3 +0.7 +0.4 -1.2 -0.3 -1.2 +1.1  0.9</p>
<p>TOT STCK BAL  -0.3 -1.6 +1.0 +1.3 -1.4 -0.2 -1.6  1.7  1.4</p>
<p> FSU NET EXP    2.4  2.0  2.7  2.6  2.2  2.4  2.4  2.9  2.8  2.3  2.6  2.5  2.7</p>
<p>* Implied call on OPEC crude equals total demand minus total non-OPEC supply minus OPEC NGLs. Thus includes &quot;miscellaneous to balance&quot; for historical time periods.</p>
<p>Figures have been adjusted to take account of Gabon's departure from OPEC, ratified at the group's 100th ministerial meeting in Vienna in June but effective from January 1995.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
